WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:13.250
Benjamin Payne: So first I don’t—this
gentleman and the folks at Hillsdale College

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:18.990
don’t ask for much recognition but I don’t
want to… I can’t stress enough the integral

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:24.150
role that they played in the success of the
school, the support of the students, the support

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:29.060
of the faculty and the support of the school’s
mission and vision. So for a few more words—he’s

00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:36.060
a much better speaker than I—Dr. Larry P.
Arnn, the President of Hillsdale College.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:47.120
Larry P. Arnn: Thank you all for coming here
and for being what you are. I can say on behalf

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:52.210
of the college that I am proud to be here with
you. I’m proud to be here with Ben and with

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:58.570
Roger. Ah, talking into the wrong microphone.
If you didn’t hear that it wasn’t very

00:00:58.570 --> 00:01:08.130
good. Ben Payne is an inspiring man and Roger,
who’s about to retire from the chairmanship

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:18.470
of the board—I think now is the right time for
us all to say “Boooooo”. You should know

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:24.649
that the arrangement the college has
with this school is that five cents or never

00:01:24.649 --> 00:01:30.920
as much as that will ever come from this school
to Hillsdale College. Why would we do that?

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:35.009
We helped to train the teachers and we know
something about the curriculum and we want

00:01:35.009 --> 00:01:41.289
to be of support. We have sent our precious
Kayla Cash, a recent graduate, down here to

00:01:41.289 --> 00:01:47.700
work in the school and you’ll find that
she’s an inspiring young woman and not so

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:56.399
great as her mother. But why? There’s going
to be beauty here. And the students are going

00:01:56.399 --> 00:02:01.880
to learn that the expression “beauty”
means the highest form of the term good and

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:07.369
they’re going to learn what that is. They’re
going to look at the old books that first

00:02:07.369 --> 00:02:11.920
talked about that—a chance to go back to
the beginning when human beings began to figure

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:17.879
this out. They’re going to learn that they
are something and that that something, when

00:02:17.879 --> 00:02:23.769
is excellent, practices those virtues that
they wear on their backs. And you mothers

00:02:23.769 --> 00:02:28.370
and grandmothers and aunts and uncles—you
should know that one of those virtues is courage

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:34.730
and courage is a hard virtue. It demands that
you do difficult things like the difficult

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:40.280
thing that you do in taking on the raising
of these young people. There’s a sacrifice

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:46.540
in that and a commitment in that that makes
life harder and more complicated. And there

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:53.510
are reasons you do that. And those are the
best reasons in human soul. A lot of you live

00:02:53.510 --> 00:02:59.549
in difficult circumstances, I know. And I
know that you worked to overcome those. And

00:02:59.549 --> 00:03:04.980
the sign of that is these young people that
are here. And these young people are going

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:11.510
to grow up in those circumstances, and yet
every one of them is fully a human being,

00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:19.629
fully capable of living a human life. The
greatest public man that I know attended school

00:03:19.629 --> 00:03:27.700
right in there and he was just like one of
these kids. He was smart, he was young, he

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:33.530
didn’t know anything, and what’s happened
to him? He sits on the Supreme Court of the

00:03:33.530 --> 00:03:39.099
United States. And how does he do that? I
have a privilege in having known him before

00:03:39.099 --> 00:03:49.389
he became a famous man. He is a good man.
He tries so hard to do the right thing and

00:03:49.389 --> 00:03:56.389
that has carried him so far. Every one of
these young people is capable of living as

00:03:56.859 --> 00:04:05.069
well as that man lives. And they have a right
to the chance. I’ll tell you one little

00:04:05.069 --> 00:04:10.999
story about Ben Payne and then I’ll shut
up. I came down and walked around this school

00:04:10.999 --> 00:04:17.999
for a day and it is true they don’t know
how to organize events here. So they think

00:04:18.209 --> 00:04:23.030
when somebody from out of town comes in, they
have to take him to a fancy restaurant. And

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:28.349
I said to Payne over there. I said “Are
you not serving lunch in this school today?”

00:04:28.349 --> 00:04:33.550
And he said “Well, we are. Hot dogs.”
They were pretty good. And I said, “Well,

00:04:33.550 --> 00:04:37.430
this is the place to have lunch. This is actually
where we ought to be having lunch today.”

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:43.090
But they still haven’t learned what they
need to know, right? And they—and I sat

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:50.990
with the students and I watched him talk with
them. And I talked with them myself. And he’s

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:59.580
just a... I said to him once. I said, “So
most of these kids grow up with uncertainty

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:04.720
and trouble, right?” And he said, “Yeah.”
And I said, “And that’s got to be made

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:12.180
up for with their families. Can this be done?”
And Ben looked at me and said “Well, Dr.

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:18.680
Arnn. We’re here. What are we going to do?”
Right? And the answer is, just like everybody

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:26.090
standing here today with a threatening rain,
we’re going to do everything we can and

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:34.400
we are going to do the right thing. I ask
you to help with that. It’s going to be

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:42.259
exhausting. It is hard to learn if you really
learn. You know, these kids are going to study

00:05:42.259 --> 00:05:49.789
Latin and that’s not easy. And yet when
they learn it—and they can all learn it,

00:05:49.789 --> 00:05:55.660
and nearly all of them will—they are going
to be different people when they have mastered

00:05:55.660 --> 00:06:03.199
that. They are going to be more fully human
with every passing day. There’s a world

00:06:03.199 --> 00:06:11.020
of blessings open to them. All it takes is
some work. I thank you for doing that work

00:06:11.020 --> 00:06:16.030
and I want you to understand how honored we
are to be able to help with it. Thanks.

